  "description": "NaLiO crystallizes in the tetragonal I4/mmm space group. Na is bonded to four equivalent O atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing NaO₄ tetrahedra. There are two shorter (2.34 Å) and two longer (2.44 Å) Na-O bond lengths. Li is bonded in a linear geometry to two equivalent O atoms. Both Li-O bond lengths are 1.81 Å. O is bonded to four equivalent Na and two equivalent Li atoms to form a mixture of distorted corner and edge-sharing ONa₄Li₂ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 8-27°.",
